From 5dfcc28e21ca02177a859f5c568b1499e335b0c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:18:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Refresh co-located beacons once an interface is set up

The Reduced Neighbor Report element of a 2.4 or 5 GHz BSS describes the
co-located 6 GHz BSSs of the same hostapd process, including their
BSSIDs. When the interfaces are brought up together, the earlier ones
build their Beacon frames while a later interface has no BSSID yet, and
only the interface that just completed its setup got its beacons
updated. The others kept announcing the 6 GHz BSS with BSSID
00:00:00:00:00:00 until something unrelated changed their beacons.

Refresh the beacons of the other interfaces too, as is already done when
an interface is enabled or disabled from the control interface.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index a4394f73d..b1a8c63cd 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -2853,8 +2853,12 @@ dfs_offload:
 	for (j = 0; j < iface->num_bss; j++)
 		hostapd_neighbor_set_own_report(iface->bss[j]);
 
-	if (iface->interfaces && iface->interfaces->count > 1)
+	if (iface->interfaces && iface->interfaces->count > 1) {
 		ieee802_11_update_beacons(iface);
+		/* The other interfaces' RNR describe this one and were built
+		 * before its BSSID was known. */
+		hostapd_refresh_all_iface_beacons(iface);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 
